nodes.body:
@hiyouga @codemayq — would one of you be able to take a look at this when you have a moment?

The change is confined to `src/llamafactory/model/model_utils/longlora.py`: the device-type check only compared against `"cuda"`, so the longlora path skipped its own handling on other accelerators. It now treats any non-CPU device the same way. One file, no behaviour change on CUDA.

Happy to adjust anything if the approach doesn't fit how you'd like this handled.

